00:48:43.220 --> 00:48:45.130
But, but I want to go out.

00:48:45.130 --> 00:48:47.730
I mean, I feel much, much better, and I need to stretch my legs.

00:48:47.730 --> 00:48:48.630
Okay, okay, okay.

00:48:48.630 --> 00:48:51.130
For a little while, though, but you should be resting.

00:48:51.130 --> 00:48:52.530
Okay, well, I won't be long.

00:48:52.530 --> 00:48:56.350
Okay.

00:48:56.350 --> 00:48:58.900
I feel so much better.

00:49:00.600 --> 00:49:02.040
Big Bird, I was just coming to see you.

00:49:02.040 --> 00:49:02.660
How are you feeling?

00:49:02.660 --> 00:49:03.410
Oh, hi, Gordon.

00:49:03.410 --> 00:49:04.830
Oh, I feel much better.

00:49:04.830 --> 00:49:07.990
Susan says my fever's gone, and I could take a little walk.

00:49:07.990 --> 00:49:09.490
For a little walk.

00:49:09.490 --> 00:49:11.110
OK, just a little walk.

00:49:13.030 --> 00:49:14.570
Hello, Bird.

00:49:14.570 --> 00:49:16.350
You're out and about.

00:49:16.350 --> 00:49:18.280
Well, I feel a lot better.

00:49:18.280 --> 00:49:19.570
I'm much better.

00:49:19.570 --> 00:49:21.050
Oh, good.

00:49:21.050 --> 00:49:25.090
Well, we're back from our picnic, and my mommy and Alice

00:49:25.090 --> 00:49:25.990
went home.

00:49:25.990 --> 00:49:30.000
But I just had to come here and tell you what happened.

00:49:30.580 --> 00:49:31.980
Well, what happened?

00:49:32.430 --> 00:49:35.380
Our balloon flew away.

00:49:36.010 --> 00:49:37.180
What do you mean?

00:49:37.340 --> 00:49:40.860
Well, Alice and I were running along,

00:49:41.120 --> 00:49:42.220
and Alice tripped,

00:49:42.520 --> 00:49:45.460
and we both lost hold of the balloon,

00:49:45.620 --> 00:49:47.420
and it flew away.

00:49:47.620 --> 00:49:48.840
Oh, well, then what happened?

00:49:48.940 --> 00:49:51.860
It went higher and higher and then disappeared.

00:49:52.780 --> 00:49:53.960
Oh, and then what happened?

00:49:53.960 --> 00:49:56.070
I wonder where it went.

00:49:56.360 --> 00:49:57.620
I don't know, Bert.

00:49:58.090 --> 00:49:59.730
Maybe it went to a...

00:50:00.000 --> 00:50:01.780
- Another planet!

00:50:01.780 --> 00:50:06.160
- Wow, I wonder if we'll ever see it again.

00:50:06.160 --> 00:50:08.530
- Bird, back to your nest.

00:50:08.530 --> 00:50:10.070
- Oh, okay.

00:50:10.070 --> 00:50:11.070
- Go ahead.

00:50:11.070 --> 00:50:12.310
- Hey Snuffy, you come with me.

00:50:12.310 --> 00:50:13.870
I want to hear everything that happens.

00:50:13.870 --> 00:50:16.870
- Sesame Street has been brought to you today

00:50:16.870 --> 00:50:20.260
by the letters B and D.

00:50:20.260 --> 00:50:21.220
- And Snuffy?

00:50:21.220 --> 00:50:22.000
- What?

00:50:22.000 --> 00:50:23.780
- Was the number the number A?

00:50:23.780 --> 00:50:25.320
- You got it, Bird.

00:50:25.320 --> 00:50:26.880
- Oh, I was hoping.

00:50:34.250 --> 00:50:35.250
Woof! Woof!

00:51:56.650 --> 00:51:59.060
Sesame Street is a production of--

00:51:59.060 --> 00:52:00.000
I know, I know.

00:52:00.000 --> 00:52:03.340
You know, the children's television workshop, right?

00:52:03.340 --> 00:52:04.980
Yeah!

00:52:04.980 --> 00:52:06.630
We're smart.

00:52:06.630 --> 00:52:07.330
You are.
